<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Observe mode configuration.

    shouldDefaultToObserveMode="true" tells the NFC system this service prefers observe mode, so
    the stack enables it whenever this service is the preferred foreground service.  Polling
    frames then arrive via processPollingFrames(); the service calls
    NfcAdapter.setObserveModeEnabled(false) exactly once per field session, and only after the
    OMAPI session is ready, to let a transaction through.

    About the AID list below.

    Android has no catch-all AID filter: CardEmulation.isValidAid() requires at least five bytes,
    so "A0*" cannot be registered.  What is declared here is therefore only a baseline of Secure
    Element development AIDs; anything else the developer needs is registered at runtime from the
    activity via CardEmulation.registerAidsForService() (see AidRegistry).  A dynamic group
    replaces the static group of the same category, so the runtime list is always the complete
    one.

    Payment RIDs (A000000003* and friends) are deliberately absent.  AOSP
    PreferredServices.isForegroundAllowedLocked() refuses preferred-service registration to a
    foreground service whose category-other AIDs collide with the default payment app when the
    NFC setting is "use default: always" — which would silently break the entire app on any
    phone with a wallet installed.  They are available as an opt-in preset in the UI instead.

    Safety: the service stays in observe mode (the firmware does not answer readers) unless
    setObserveModeEnabled(false) is called, which happens only when the user has pressed Start,
    the OMAPI session is established, and an ISO-DEP reader is actually polling.

    See ref_aosp/NfcNci/src/com/android/nfc/cardemulation/HostEmulationManager.java for how the
    stack processes observe mode and polling frames.
-->
<host-apdu-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/servicedesc"
    android:requireDeviceUnlock="true"
    android:shouldDefaultToObserveMode="true">

    <!-- Keep in sync with AidRegistry.DEFAULT_AIDS. -->
    <aid-group android:description="@string/aiddescription" android:category="other">
        <aid-filter android:name="A000000151*"/>  <!-- GlobalPlatform Issuer Security Domain -->
        <aid-filter android:name="A000000087*"/>  <!-- 3GPP USIM / ISIM -->
        <aid-filter android:name="A000000063*"/>  <!-- PKCS#15 -->
        <aid-filter android:name="A000000647*"/>  <!-- FIDO -->
        <aid-filter android:name="D276000085*"/>  <!-- NDEF Type 4 Tag -->
        <aid-filter android:name="F000000000*"/>  <!-- Proprietary -->
        <aid-filter android:name="F000000001*"/>
        <aid-filter android:name="F000000002*"/>
        <aid-filter android:name="F000000003*"/>
    </aid-group>
</host-apdu-service>
